{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (config_006, 0.653) is the clear best so far, and multiprofile provides a ~13% boost over single profile. Image alone (resnet50) is very weak (0.208), so it's uncertain whether adding it provides any complementary signal. Question: Does fusing image (resnet50) via concat with the best RNA multiprofile model (scvi_n200, transformer) improve upon the 0.653 RNA-only baseline? This is the highest-value test because it directly probes whether multimodality can push past the current ceiling using the best-known components. Using concat (simpler) and resnet50 (the only image encoder with prior data) keeps the comparison clean. If multimodal helps, the remaining 3 experiments can explore weighted fusion and imagenet_vit_l; if it doesn't, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and conserve budget. This is the best use of experiment 7 because it tests the single most impactful unexplored direction (adding a second modality to the best RNA setup) with minimal confounding variables."
}

